# --- ANCHOR rows (6th column): PUBLISHED values, never refreshed by --record -
# Hamer & Wu, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 1 (1972) 1047, DOI 10.1063/1.3253108
# (NBS critically-evaluated tables, 25 C).  Every number below is the PAPER's,
# transcribed from constant/experiments/hamer_wu_1972.dat, not the model's.
#
# WHAT THESE ADD, given the diag rows above already pin every quantity at
# 1e-4.  Those rows are SELF-RECORDED: they catch drift of any size, against
# Choupo's own last answer.  They cannot catch a Choupo that was never right,
# and they carry no link to the measurement at all -- the agreement lived only
# in the propsDict header, which is prose, and prose goes stale silently.
# The anchor rows carry the link, as data.
#
# THE BAND IS 2 % ON ALL FIFTEEN ROWS, deliberately ONE band and deliberately
# not the observed error.  Observed when authored (2026-08-10), gamma_pm at
# 1 m / 3 m and phi at 1 m:
#     NaCl  +0.03 %  0.00 %  +0.03 %
#     KCl   +0.05 % +0.32 %  +0.08 %
#     KBr   -0.28 % -0.17 %  +0.01 %
#     HCl   +0.06 % +0.16 %  +0.21 %
#     NaOH  -0.90 % -1.28 %  -0.72 %   <-- the loosest, and a REPORTED finding
# Four of the five sit inside 0.35 %; NaOH is 4x worse and the band was not
# set from it (1.5 % would also have held).  A 2 % anchor therefore says only
# "the answer has not left the published table", which is what an anchor is
# for; it does NOT certify the 0.1 % agreement the tight salts show, and it
# is NOT a declared accuracy envelope for Pitzer 1-1 salts -- that taxonomy
# is roadmap (docs/design/post-consolidation-roadmap.md item 3).
#
# LiCl IS ABSENT ON PURPOSE.  The catalogue Li-Cl pair was REFIT to this very
# table, so an anchor row on it would claim validation from the data the
# parameters already saw -- the exact circularity the evidence taxonomy is
# meant to make machine-detectable.  Its diag rows above stay: as a
# fit-consistency check they are honest, and at ~3 % they are also the
# corpus's own evidence that three Pitzer parameters cannot hold LiCl across
# two anchors.  A row omitted with its reason is worth more than a row that
# passes for the wrong one.
